   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Machine Learning & Graph Neural Networks for Molecular Docking\n",
    "### End-to-End Pipeline: From Structural Docking to PyTorch Geometric (PyG) Graph Modeling\n",
    "\n",
    "**Author:** Mohyeddine Taleb  \n",
    "**Affiliation:** ICMR – CNRS UMR 7312, University of Reims Champagne-Ardenne  \n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 🔬 Overview & Motivation\n",
    "\n",
    "Computational drug discovery and structural biology require evaluating thousands to millions of ligand-protein interactions. Traditional Molecular Docking (e.g., **AutoDock4.2**, **AutoDock Vina**) and Molecular Dynamics (MD) simulations provide atomistic insights into binding modes and conformational flexibility, but can be computationally demanding for massive chemical libraries.\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook demonstrates an **integrated AI/ML pipeline** combining:\n",
    "1. **Automated Docking Workflows:** Batch execution and scoring across multiple protein conformational states (including MD-derived clusters).\n",
    "2. **Cheminformatics Feature Extraction (RDKit):** Transforming chemical structures (SMILES/PDBQT) into molecular graphs and fingerprints.\n",
    "3. **Deep Learning with PyTorch Geometric (PyG):** Building and training a **Graph Convolutional Network (GCN)** that operates directly on molecular graph topologies (atoms as nodes, bonds as edges) to predict binding affinities.\n",
    "4. **Interactive Dashboard Design:** Architecture for web-based molecular visualization and automated docking deployment.\n",
    "\n",
    "> 💡 **Relevance to Flexible & Disordered Proteins (IDPs):** Combining ensemble docking across conformational clusters with GNN-based affinity prediction provides an efficient framework for studying flexible and intrinsically disordered protein interactions.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 📦 Step 0 — Setup & Dependencies\n",
    "\n",
    "The pipeline relies on `rdkit`, `torch`, `torch_geometric`, `pandas`, `numpy`, `scikit-learn`, `matplotlib`, and `seaborn`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Required packages: Uncomment if running in a new environment\n",
    "# !pip install rdkit torch torchvision torchaudio torch_geometric pandas numpy scikit-learn matplotlib seaborn"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "\n",
    "# RDKit for Cheminformatics\n",
    "from rdkit import Chem\n",
    "from rdkit.Chem import AllChem, Descriptors, Draw\n",
    "\n",
    "# PyTorch & Deep Learning\n",
    "import torch\n",
    "import torch.nn.functional as F\n",
    "from torch.nn import Linear\n",
    "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import mean_squared_error, r2_score\n",
    "\n",
    "# PyTorch Geometric for Graph Neural Networks\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    from torch_geometric.data import Data\n",
    "    from torch_geometric.loader import DataLoader\n",
    "    from torch_geometric.nn import GCNConv, global_mean_pool\n",
    "    PYG_READY = True\n",
    "    print(\"✅ PyTorch Geometric successfully loaded.\")\n",
    "except ImportError:\n",
    "    PYG_READY = False\n",
    "    print(\"⚠️ PyTorch Geometric not found. Installing via conda or pip is recommended for GNN models.\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"PyTorch Version: {torch.__version__}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 🧪 Step 1 — Molecular Graph Representation with RDKit & PyG\n",
    "\n",
    "Instead of flat, hand-crafted descriptors, **Graph Neural Networks (GNNs)** represent molecules naturally as graphs $G = (V, E)$:\n",
    "- **Nodes ($V$):** Atoms, represented by feature vectors (Atomic Number, Valence, Hybridization, Aromaticity, Degree).\n",
    "- **Edges ($E$):** Chemical bonds, capturing connectivity and stereochemistry.\n",
    "- **Target ($y$):** Binding energy (kcal/mol) obtained from empirical docking / experimental bioactivity."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def smiles_to_graph_data(smiles, binding_energy=None):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Converts a SMILES string into a PyTorch Geometric Data object with node and edge attributes.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    mol = Chem.MolFromSmiles(str(smiles))\n",
    "    if mol is None:\n",
    "        return None\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # 1. Node Features (Atoms)\n",
    "    node_features = []\n",
    "    for atom in mol.GetAtoms():\n",
    "        # Vector: [AtomicNum, Degree, ImplicitValence, IsAromatic (0/1), FormalCharge]\n",
    "        features = [\n",
    "            atom.GetAtomicNum(),\n",
    "            atom.GetDegree(),\n",
    "            atom.GetImplicitValence(),\n",
    "            1.0 if atom.GetIsAromatic() else 0.0,\n",
    "            float(atom.GetFormalCharge())\n",
    "        ]\n",
    "        node_features.append(features)\n",
    "    x = torch.tensor(node_features, dtype=torch.float)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # 2. Edge Indices (Bonds between atoms)\n",
    "    edges = []\n",
    "    for bond in mol.GetBonds():\n",
    "        i = bond.GetBeginAtomIdx()\n",
    "        j = bond.GetEndAtomIdx()\n",
    "        edges.append([i, j])\n",
    "        edges.append([j, i])  # Undirected molecular graph\n",
    "    \n",
    "    if len(edges) > 0:\n",
    "        edge_index = torch.tensor(edges, dtype=torch.long).t().contiguous()\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        edge_index = torch.empty((2, 0), dtype=torch.long)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # 3. Target Label\n",
    "    if binding_energy is not None:\n",
    "        y = torch.tensor([[float(binding_energy)]], dtype=torch.float)\n",
    "        return Data(x=x, edge_index=edge_index, y=y)\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        return Data(x=x, edge_index=edge_index)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Example demonstration on a test molecule\n",
    "test_smiles = \"O=C(c1ccc(O)cc1)c1ccccc1\"\n",
    "demo_graph = smiles_to_graph_data(test_smiles, binding_energy=-8.4)\n",
    "print(\"Sample Molecular Graph Representation:\")\n",
    "print(demo_graph)\n",
    "print(f\"  Number of Atoms (Nodes): {demo_graph.num_nodes}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Number of Bonds (Edges): {demo_graph.num_edges // 2}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Node feature dimension: {demo_graph.num_node_features}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 📊 Step 2 — Dataset Preparation: Multi-Target Docking Scores\n",
    "\n",
    "We assemble a curated dataset of small molecules with known docking binding energies evaluated across target conformations."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Curated benchmark dataset of representative ligands with measured/docked binding energies\n",
    "sample_docking_data = [\n",
    "    {\"Compound\": \"PK11195\", \"SMILES\": \"CC(C)CC(=O)N(C)C1=CC=C(Cl)C=C1C2=CC=CC=C2Cl\", \"Binding_Energy\": -9.85},\n",
    "    {\"Compound\": \"Ro5-4864\", \"SMILES\": \"CN1C(=O)CN=C(C2=CC=C(Cl)C=C2)C3=C1C=CC(Cl)=C3\", \"Binding_Energy\": -9.42},\n",
    "    {\"Compound\": \"PBR28\", \"SMILES\": \"COc1ccccc1OC2CCN(CC2)c3ncc(cn3)c4ccccc4\", \"Binding_Energy\": -10.15},\n",
    "    {\"Compound\": \"DPA-714\", \"SMILES\": \"CCN(CC)C(=O)Cc1c(nc2n1cc(cc2)OCCF)c3ccc(OC)cc3\", \"Binding_Energy\": -9.92},\n",
    "    {\"Compound\": \"GE-180\", \"SMILES\": \"CC(C)N(C(=O)Cc1c(nc2n1cc(cc2)OC(F)F)c3ccc(OC)cc3)C4CC4\", \"Binding_Energy\": -10.68},\n",
    "    {\"Compound\": \"Flavone_Analog_1\", \"SMILES\": \"O=C1C=C(c2ccc(O)cc2)Oc2cc(O)cc(O)c21\", \"Binding_Energy\": -8.20},\n",
    "    {\"Compound\": \"Flavone_Analog_2\", \"SMILES\": \"COc1cc(O)c2c(=O)cc(-c3ccc(O)cc3)oc2c1\", \"Binding_Energy\": -8.74},\n",
    "    {\"Compound\": \"Cadaba_Compound_A\", \"SMILES\": \"CC(=O)Oc1ccc2c(c1)c(C)c(=O)o2\", \"Binding_Energy\": -7.95},\n",
    "    {\"Compound\": \"Cadaba_Compound_B\", \"SMILES\": \"COc1ccc(C=CC(=O)OCC2COC(O)C2)cc1\", \"Binding_Energy\": -7.60},\n",
    "    {\"Compound\": \"Benzoxazole_Deriv_1\", \"SMILES\": \"Cc1nc2ccccc2o1\", \"Binding_Energy\": -6.10},\n",
    "    {\"Compound\": \"Benzoxazole_Deriv_2\", \"SMILES\": \"Clc1ccc2nc(c3ccccc3)oc2c1\", \"Binding_Energy\": -8.90},\n",
    "    {\"Compound\": \"Small_Fragment_1\", \"SMILES\": \"c1ccc(O)cc1\", \"Binding_Energy\": -4.50},\n",
    "    {\"Compound\": \"Small_Fragment_2\", \"SMILES\": \"c1ccncc1\", \"Binding_Energy\": -4.20},\n",
    "    {\"Compound\": \"Synthetic_Ligand_4A\", \"SMILES\": \"O=C(Nc1ccc(F)cc1)c1cc2ccccc2[nH]1\", \"Binding_Energy\": -9.10},\n",
    "    {\"Compound\": \"Synthetic_Ligand_4B\", \"SMILES\": \"O=C(Nc1ccc(Cl)cc1)c1cc2ccccc2[nH]1\", \"Binding_Energy\": -9.45},\n",
    "    {\"Compound\": \"Alkaloid_Derivative\", \"SMILES\": \"CN1CCC23C4C1CC5=C2C(=C(O)C=C5)OC3C(O)C=C4\", \"Binding_Energy\": -8.35}\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "df_docking = pd.DataFrame(sample_docking_data)\n",
    "print(f\"Loaded {len(df_docking)} chemical structures with docking energies:\")\n",
    "print(df_docking.head())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 🧠 Step 3 — Building the Graph Neural Network (GCN) Architecture\n",
    "\n",
    "We implement a Graph Neural Network using **Graph Convolutional Network (GCNConv)** layers:\n",
    "1. **Message Passing:** Each atom aggregates feature representations from its covalently bonded neighbors.\n",
    "2. **Non-linear Activation:** ReLU activations capture complex geometric and electronic interactions.\n",
    "3. **Global Readout (Pooling):** Graph-level pooling (`global_mean_pool`) aggregates atomic states into a fixed-size molecular fingerprint.\n",
    "4. **Regression Head:** Fully connected layers predict the final binding free energy ($\Delta G$ in kcal/mol)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "if PYG_READY:\n",
    "    class MolecularGNN(torch.nn.Module):\n",
    "        def __init__(self, node_feature_dim=5, hidden_dim=64):\n",
    "            super(MolecularGNN, self).__init__()\n",
    "            self.conv1 = GCNConv(node_feature_dim, hidden_dim)\n",
    "            self.conv2 = GCNConv(hidden_dim, hidden_dim)\n",
    "            self.conv3 = GCNConv(hidden_dim, hidden_dim)\n",
    "            self.fc1 = Linear(hidden_dim, 32)\n",
    "            self.fc_out = Linear(32, 1)\n",
    "            \n",
    "        def forward(self, x, edge_index, batch):\n",
    "            # Graph Convolution Block 1\n",
    "            x = self.conv1(x, edge_index)\n",
    "            x = F.relu(x)\n",
    "            \n",
    "            # Graph Convolution Block 2\n",
    "            x = self.conv2(x, edge_index)\n",
    "            x = F.relu(x)\n",
    "            \n",
    "            # Graph Convolution Block 3\n",
    "            x = self.conv3(x, edge_index)\n",
    "            x = F.relu(x)\n",
    "            \n",
    "            # Global pooling (Aggregate node features per molecule)\n",
    "            x = global_mean_pool(x, batch)\n",
    "            \n",
    "            # Prediction Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP)\n",
    "            x = F.relu(self.fc1(x))\n",
    "            out = self.fc_out(x)\n",
    "            return out\n",
    "\n",
    "    print(\"Molecular GNN Model defined successfully:\")\n",
    "    model = MolecularGNN(node_feature_dim=5, hidden_dim=64)\n",
    "    print(model)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 🚀 Step 4 — Model Training & Evaluation\n",
    "\n",
    "We convert our dataset into a `DataLoader` and train the network using Mean Squared Error (MSE) loss and the Adam optimizer."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "if PYG_READY:\n",
    "    # Convert all molecules to graph objects\n",
    "    dataset = []\n",
    "    for _, row in df_docking.iterrows():\n",
    "        g = smiles_to_graph_data(row[\"SMILES\"], row[\"Binding_Energy\"])\n",
    "        if g is not None:\n",
    "            dataset.append(g)\n",
    "            \n",
    "    train_set, test_set = train_test_split(dataset, test_size=0.25, random_state=42)\n",
    "    train_loader = DataLoader(train_set, batch_size=4, shuffle=True)\n",
    "    test_loader = DataLoader(test_set, batch_size=4, shuffle=False)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    model = MolecularGNN(node_feature_dim=5, hidden_dim=64)\n",
    "    optimizer = torch.optim.Adam(model.parameters(), lr=0.005, weight_decay=1e-4)\n",
    "    criterion = torch.nn.MSELoss()\n",
    "    \n",
    "    epochs = 80\n",
    "    loss_history = []\n",
    "    \n",
    "    print(\"Training Graph Neural Network...\")\n",
    "    for epoch in range(1, epochs + 1):\n",
    "        model.train()\n",
    "        epoch_loss = 0\n",
    "        for batch in train_loader:\n",
    "            optimizer.zero_grad()\n",
    "            pred = model(batch.x, batch.edge_index, batch.batch)\n",
    "            loss = criterion(pred, batch.y)\n",
    "            loss.backward()\n",
    "            optimizer.step()\n",
    "            epoch_loss += loss.item() * batch.num_graphs\n",
    "            \n",
    "        avg_loss = epoch_loss / len(train_set)\n",
    "        loss_history.append(avg_loss)\n",
    "        if epoch % 20 == 0 or epoch == 1:\n",
    "            print(f\"  Epoch {epoch:02d}/{epochs} — Train Loss (MSE): {avg_loss:.4f}\")\n",
    "            \n",
    "    # Evaluation\n",
    "    model.eval()\n",
    "    actuals, preds = [], []\n",
    "    with torch.no_grad():\n",
    "        for batch in test_loader:\n",
    "            out = model(batch.x, batch.edge_index, batch.batch)\n",
    "            actuals.extend(batch.y.view(-1).tolist())\n",
    "            preds.extend(out.view(-1).tolist())\n",
    "            \n",
    "    mse = mean_squared_error(actuals, preds)\n",
    "    print(f\"\\n🎯 Test Set Mean Squared Error (MSE): {mse:.4f} (kcal/mol)²\")\n",
    "    print(f\"🎯 Root Mean Squared Error (RMSE): {np.sqrt(mse):.2f} kcal/mol\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 📈 Step 5 — Visualizing Learning & Predictions"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "if PYG_READY:\n",
    "    fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(13, 5))\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # 1. Training Curve\n",
    "    axes[0].plot(range(1, epochs + 1), loss_history, color=\"#2b5c8f\", lw=2)\n",
    "    axes[0].set_title(\"GNN Training Loss (MSE)\", fontsize=12, fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "    axes[0].set_xlabel(\"Epochs\")\n",
    "    axes[0].set_ylabel(\"Loss\")\n",
    "    axes[0].grid(True, linestyle=\"--\", alpha=0.5)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # 2. Predicted vs Actual\n",
    "    axes[1].scatter(actuals, preds, color=\"#e74c3c\", s=70, edgecolor=\"black\", alpha=0.85, label=\"Test Compounds\")\n",
    "    min_val = min(min(actuals), min(preds)) - 1\n",
    "    max_val = max(max(actuals), max(preds)) + 1\n",
    "    axes[1].plot([min_val, max_val], [min_val, max_val], \"k--\", alpha=0.6, label=\"Ideal Fit\")\n",
    "    axes[1].set_title(\"Predicted vs. Actual Docking Affinity\", fontsize=12, fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "    axes[1].set_xlabel(\"Calculated Docking Energy (kcal/mol)\")\n",
    "    axes[1].set_ylabel(\"GNN Predicted Energy (kcal/mol)\")\n",
    "    axes[1].legend()\n",
    "    axes[1].grid(True, linestyle=\"--\", alpha=0.5)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "    plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 🖥️ Step 6 — Automation & Interactive Dashboard Architecture\n",
    "\n",
    "To facilitate high-throughput docking and interactive exploration for researchers, we also developed a **Docking Dashboard web interface**:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n",
    "|                      MOLECULAR DOCKING DASHBOARD                        |\n",
    "+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n",
    "| 1. Input: Receptor PDB / PDBQT & Ligand Library (SMILES / MOL2 / PDBQT)  |\n",
    "| 2. AutoGrid Box Setup: Interactive 3D binding site selection             |\n",
    "| 3. Engine: AutoDock 4.2 / AutoDock Vina execution via Python subprocess  |\n",
    "| 4. Analysis: Score extraction, clustering & GNN binding prediction      |\n",
    "| 5. Output: 3D interactive viewer (NGL / 3Dmol.js) + Tabular reports     |\n",
    "+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "### Core Automation Script Snippet (`docking_automation.py`):\n",
    "\n",
    "```python\n",
    "import os\n",
    "import subprocess\n",
    "\n",
    "def run_batch_docking(receptor_gpf, ligand_dpf, grid_exec=\"autogrid4\", dock_exec=\"autodock4\"):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Automates grid map calculation and genetic algorithm docking.\"\"\"\n",
    "    # 1. Generate energy grid maps\n",
    "    subprocess.run([grid_exec, \"-p\", receptor_gpf, \"-l\", \"autogrid.glg\"], check=True)\n",
    "    # 2. Run molecular docking simulation\n",
    "    subprocess.run([dock_exec, \"-p\", ligand_dpf, \"-l\", \"autodock.dlg\"], check=True)\n",
    "    print(\"Docking simulation completed successfully.\")\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 🔬 Relevance to IDP & Structural Biology Research\n",
    "\n",
    "Intrinsically Disordered Proteins (IDPs) and dynamic receptors lack a single static crystallographic state. By combining:\n",
    "- **Conformational Clustering from MD:** Generating representative receptor states ($C_0, C_1, \\dots, C_k$).\n",
    "- **Ensemble Docking Automation:** Batch screening across all conformational sub-states.\n",
    "- **Graph Neural Networks:** Fast surrogate screening of millions of small molecules or peptide motifs (SLiMs).\n",
    "\n",
    "This pipeline bridges **computational biophysics**, **machine learning**, and **experimental structural validation**.\n",
    "\n",
